  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','A Yoruba proverb says ''Àgbà kì í wà lọ́jà kí orí ọmọ tuntun wọ́''. What good value does it teach?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Elders should care for and guide the young"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Markets should close early"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Children should not go to school"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Babies should carry loads"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "This Yoruba proverb teaches that elders present should guide and protect the young, so nothing goes wrong."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','The Igbo proverb ''Onye aghala nwanne ya'' teaches us to do what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Forget your family"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Not abandon your brother or sister"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fight with friends"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Keep all your food"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Igbo proverb ''Onye aghala nwanne ya'' means one should not abandon their sibling, teaching unity and care."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','A Hausa proverb ''Hakuri maganin duniya'' praises which good behaviour?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Being greedy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Being patient"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Being lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Being noisy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Hakuri maganin duniya'' means patience is the medicine of the world, praising patience."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','Many Nigerian proverbs about the ''ant'' or hard work teach children to be what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hardworking"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Selfish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rude"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Careless"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Proverbs about ants and hard work teach children to be hardworking."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','A proverb is a wise saying. In Yoruba, a proverb is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Òwe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Orin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ìtàn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Àlọ́"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In Yoruba, a proverb is called ''òwe''."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','The popular children''s song ''Omo mi w''ẹ̀hìn'' is sung in which Nigerian language?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "d", "text": "English"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Omo mi w''ẹ̀hìn'' is a well-known Yoruba children''s song."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','In Yoruba, what is the word for a ''song''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Orin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Òwe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ìwé"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ọjà"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Orin'' is the Yoruba word for ''song''."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','In Igbo, what is the word for a ''song''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Egwu"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Akwụkwọ"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nri"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ụlọ"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Egwu'' is the Igbo word for ''song'' (also used for music and dance)."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','In Hausa, what is the word for a ''song''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Waƙa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Littafi"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ruwa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Gida"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Waƙa'' is the Hausa word for ''song''."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','A folktale riddle told for fun in Yoruba culture is called an ''àlọ́''. What is it mainly used for?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Buying goods"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Teaching and entertaining children"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cooking food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Building houses"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Àlọ́'' (folktales and riddles) are used in Yoruba culture to teach lessons and entertain children."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','''Àmàlà'' is a swallow food traditionally eaten mostly among which Nigerian language group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Efik"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Àmàlà'', made from yam flour, is a food commonly associated with the Yoruba people."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','''Tuwo shinkafa'' is a rice meal popular among which Nigerian language group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ijaw"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Tuwo shinkafa'', made from rice, is a traditional Hausa meal."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','In Igbo culture, ''abacha'' (African salad) is made mainly from which crop?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rice"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cassava"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Beans"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Maize"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Abacha'' is an Igbo dish made from processed cassava."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','In Yoruba, what is the word for ''food''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Oúnjẹ"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Omi"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ilé"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Aṣọ"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Oúnjẹ'' is the Yoruba word for ''food''."}',0.25,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','''Jollof rice'' is a favourite Nigerian party food. What colour is jollof rice usually?','[{"id": "a", "text": "White"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Green"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Red or orange"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blue"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Jollof rice is cooked with tomatoes and pepper, giving it a red or orange colour."}',0.25,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','In Yoruba, the word ''aṣọ'' means what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cloth or clothing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "House"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Food"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Aṣọ'' is the Yoruba word for ''cloth'' or ''clothing''."}',0.25,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The ''agbада'' is a large flowing gown worn by men, especially among which Nigerian group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tiv"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Igala"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The ''agbada'' is a traditional flowing gown commonly worn by Yoruba men."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','In many Hausa communities, men often wear a cap called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hula"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Gele"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Isiagu"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buba"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Hula'' is the traditional Hausa cap worn by men."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The ''gele'' is a colourful head-tie worn by women, especially among the Yoruba. What is it worn on?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The feet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The head"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The hands"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The waist"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A ''gele'' is a head-tie, so it is worn on the head."}',0.3,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P1','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The ''isiagu'' patterned shirt with lion-head designs is worn traditionally by which Nigerian group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Nupe"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The ''isiagu'' is a traditional Igbo shirt, often patterned with lion-head designs."}',0.35,'{P1,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O1','Which of these is a living thing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A stone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A table"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cup"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A goat is alive because it can eat, grow and move on its own."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O1','Which of these is a non-living thing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A dog"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A mango tree"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A chair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A fish"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A chair is non-living because it cannot eat, grow or move by itself."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O1','Ada saw a bird flying in her compound. The bird is a __ thing.','[{"id": "a", "text": "living"}, {"id": "b", "text": "non-living"}, {"id": "c", "text": "plastic"}, {"id": "d", "text": "metal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A bird is a living thing because it moves, eats and grows."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O1','Which group has only non-living things?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dog, cat, cow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Book, spoon, bucket"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tree, grass, flower"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fish, hen, snake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A book, spoon and bucket are all non-living because none of them can eat or grow."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O1','Which of these is a living thing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A pencil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A ball"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A yam plant"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A shoe"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A yam plant is living because it grows and needs water and sunlight."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O2','What do all living things need to stay alive?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Food and water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Paint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Nails"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Living things need food and water to grow and stay alive."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O2','Which of these can a living thing do that a non-living thing cannot?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stay in one place"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Grow bigger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Be broken"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Be cold"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Living things can grow bigger, but non-living things cannot grow on their own."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O2','A puppy grows to become a big dog. This shows that a puppy is a __ thing.','[{"id": "a", "text": "non-living"}, {"id": "b", "text": "living"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wooden"}, {"id": "d", "text": "metal"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Only living things grow, so the puppy that grows is a living thing."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O2','Living things also need __ to breathe.','[{"id": "a", "text": "air"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "paper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cloth"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Living things need air to breathe and stay alive."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T1','BSC-T1-O2','Which sentence is TRUE about non-living things?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They eat food every day"}, {"id": "b", "text": "They grow taller each year"}, {"id": "c", "text": "They do not eat or grow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They have babies"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Non-living things do not eat or grow because they are not alive."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O1','Which part of the body do we use to see?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The ears"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The eyes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The nose"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The legs"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We use our eyes to see things around us."}',0.15,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O1','We use our __ to hear sounds.','[{"id": "a", "text": "eyes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hands"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ears"}, {"id": "d", "text": "teeth"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We use our ears to hear sounds."}',0.15,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O1','Which part of the body do we use to smell a nice pot of jollof rice?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The nose"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The knee"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The elbow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The hair"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We use our nose to smell things like food."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O1','Chidi kicks a football with his __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "ears"}, {"id": "b", "text": "legs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nose"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eyes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We use our legs to walk, run and kick a ball."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O1','We use our __ to hold a pencil and write.','[{"id": "a", "text": "feet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tongue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hands"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ears"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We use our hands to hold things and to write."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O2','What should we use to brush our teeth?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Toothbrush and toothpaste"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sand and water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Soap and towel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Comb and oil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We brush our teeth with a toothbrush and toothpaste to keep them clean."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O2','When should we wash our hands?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Only on Sundays"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Before eating and after using the toilet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only when sleeping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Never"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We wash our hands before eating and after using the toilet to stay healthy."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O2','What do we use with water to wash our body clean?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Soap"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Salt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sugar"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sand"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We use soap and water to wash dirt off our body."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O2','Ngozi''s hair is untidy. What should she use to make it neat?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A spoon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A comb"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A cup"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A plate"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We use a comb to make our hair neat and tidy."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T2','BSC-T2-O2','Why should we cut our finger nails short?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To keep dirt and germs away"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To make them longer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "So we can eat sand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "So we can be dirty"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Short, clean nails keep dirt and germs from entering our body."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O1','We breathe in __ to stay alive.','[{"id": "a", "text": "air"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wood"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We breathe in air, which our body needs to stay alive."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O1','What do we drink when we are thirsty?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Petrol"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paint"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We drink clean water when we are thirsty."}',0.15,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O1','Moving air is also called __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "wind"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fire"}, {"id": "d", "text": "soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Air that moves is called wind, and it can blow leaves and clothes."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O1','Which of these do we use water for at home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cooking and washing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reading a book"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Singing a song"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sleeping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "At home we use water for cooking, washing and drinking."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O1','Can you see the air around you?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yes, it is green"}, {"id": "b", "text": "No, but we can feel it when the wind blows"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Yes, it is red"}, {"id": "d", "text": "No, and we can never feel it"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Air cannot be seen, but we feel it when the wind blows on us."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O2','On a rainy day, what falls from the sky?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rain water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stones"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaves"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "On a rainy day, rain water falls from the clouds in the sky."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O2','What do we use to stay dry when it is raining?','[{"id": "a", "text": "An umbrella"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A pillow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A plate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A pencil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We use an umbrella or raincoat to stay dry in the rain."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O2','On a sunny day, the sky is bright and the __ shines.','[{"id": "a", "text": "sun"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "mud"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cup"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "On a sunny day the sun shines and gives us light and heat."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O2','Mama hangs wet clothes outside to dry. Which weather is best for this?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rainy weather"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sunny weather"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Foggy night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stormy weather"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sunny weather is best for drying clothes because the sun dries them fast."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T3','BSC-T3-O2','Which of these do we often see in the sky on a rainy day?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bright hot sun"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Dark clouds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Green grass"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A football"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dark clouds gather in the sky before and during the rain."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O1','A drinking glass is usually made from __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "glass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "paper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A drinking glass is made from glass, which is clear and hard."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O1','Which of these is made from wood?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A wooden chair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A glass window"}, {"id": "c", "text": "An iron nail"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A rubber tyre"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A wooden chair is made from wood that comes from trees."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O1','Our exercise books and newspapers are made from __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "iron"}, {"id": "b", "text": "paper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "glass"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Exercise books and newspapers are made from paper."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O1','Which material is a cooking pot often made from?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Paper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cloth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Metal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaves"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cooking pots are made from metal because metal does not burn easily."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O1','The clothes we wear are made from __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "cloth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "iron"}, {"id": "c", "text": "glass"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stone"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Our clothes are made from cloth, which is soft to wear."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O2','Which of these is a hard material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A stone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cotton wool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A sponge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A pillow"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stone is hard because it does not bend or press in easily."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O2','Which of these is a soft material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "An iron rod"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A block"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A soft sponge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A brick"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A sponge is soft because it presses in easily when we squeeze it."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O2','When you press a pillow, it goes in. This shows the pillow is __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "hard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "soft"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cold"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pillow is soft because it presses in when you push it."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O2','Which group has only hard things?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stone, brick, iron nail"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sponge, cotton wool, pillow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cloth, paper, feather"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Water, air, foam"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stone, brick and iron nail are all hard because none of them press in easily."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T4','BSC-T4-O2','Why do we use soft cotton wool to clean a small wound?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Because it is very hard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Because it is soft and gentle on the skin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Because it is made of iron"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Because it is heavy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cotton wool is soft and gentle, so it does not hurt the skin."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O1','What can happen if you touch a hot pressing iron?','[{"id": "a", "text": "You can get burnt"}, {"id": "b", "text": "You will grow taller"}, {"id": "c", "text": "You will sing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Nothing at all"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hot iron can burn your skin, so you should not touch it."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O1','Which of these is safe to play with in school?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A sharp knife"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A box of matches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A soft ball"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Broken glass"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A soft ball is safe to play with because it cannot cut or burn you."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O1','You should NOT play with fire or matches because they can cause __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "burns and accidents"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sweet food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "new toys"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clean water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fire and matches can cause burns and accidents, so children must not play with them."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O1','Before crossing a road in Lagos, you should first __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "close your eyes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "look left and right for cars"}, {"id": "c", "text": "run without looking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lie down on the road"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "You must look left and right for cars to cross the road safely."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O1','A bottle in the kitchen has no name on it. What should you do?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Drink it quickly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Not drink it and tell an adult"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pour it on your food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Share it with friends"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "You should never drink an unknown liquid; tell an adult to stay safe."}',0.3,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O2','Which tool is used to cut paper in the classroom?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A scissors"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A cup"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A plate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A shoe"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pair of scissors is used to cut paper and cloth."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O2','A hammer is used to __.','[{"id": "a", "text": "drive in a nail"}, {"id": "b", "text": "drink water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "read a book"}, {"id": "d", "text": "comb hair"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hammer is used to drive nails into wood."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O2','Which tool does a farmer use to dig the ground?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A hoe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A pencil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A book"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A farmer uses a hoe to dig and prepare the ground for planting."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O2','We use a __ to sweep the floor and keep it clean.','[{"id": "a", "text": "broom"}, {"id": "b", "text": "spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cup"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ruler"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We use a broom to sweep dirt off the floor."}',0.2,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','BSC','BSC-T5','BSC-T5-O2','Musa wants to draw a straight line in his book. Which tool should he use?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A ruler"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A plate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A hammer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A broom"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A ruler is used to draw straight lines and to measure length."}',0.25,'{P2,BSC,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Which of these letters is a vowel?','[{"id": "a", "text": "b"}, {"id": "b", "text": "e"}, {"id": "c", "text": "t"}, {"id": "d", "text": "m"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The five vowels are a, e, i, o and u."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','How many vowels are there in the English alphabet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "3"}, {"id": "b", "text": "7"}, {"id": "c", "text": "5"}, {"id": "d", "text": "10"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The vowels are a, e, i, o, u, which makes five."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Which letter comes right after ''g'' in the alphabet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "h"}, {"id": "b", "text": "f"}, {"id": "c", "text": "j"}, {"id": "d", "text": "e"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The order is f, g, h, so h comes after g."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Which of these letters is a consonant?','[{"id": "a", "text": "a"}, {"id": "b", "text": "o"}, {"id": "c", "text": "i"}, {"id": "d", "text": "k"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "Any letter that is not a, e, i, o or u is a consonant, like k."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Which letter comes first in the alphabet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "c"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a"}, {"id": "c", "text": "b"}, {"id": "d", "text": "d"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The alphabet begins with the letter a."}',0.15,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','Which word begins with the sound of the letter ''b''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "ball"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dog"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sun"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The word ''ball'' starts with the /b/ sound."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','What letter does the word ''mango'' begin with?','[{"id": "a", "text": "n"}, {"id": "b", "text": "m"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a"}, {"id": "d", "text": "g"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Mango'' begins with the letter m."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','Which word begins with the same sound as ''fish''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "table"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "boy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rice"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Both ''fish'' and ''fan'' start with the /f/ sound."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','What letter does the word ''yam'' begin with?','[{"id": "a", "text": "a"}, {"id": "b", "text": "m"}, {"id": "c", "text": "y"}, {"id": "d", "text": "w"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Yam'' begins with the letter y."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','Which word begins with the sound of the letter ''s''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "snake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pot"}, {"id": "c", "text": "leg"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Snake'' starts with the /s/ sound."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which of these is an animal?','[{"id": "a", "text": "chair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spoon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "book"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A goat is a farm animal."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','What do we use to write in our exercise book?','[{"id": "a", "text": "plate"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cup"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pencil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "shoe"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We use a pencil to write."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which of these is a fruit?','[{"id": "a", "text": "orange"}, {"id": "b", "text": "table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "door"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pen"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An orange is a fruit we can eat."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','What do we wear on our feet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "cap"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shoes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gloves"}, {"id": "d", "text": "belt"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We wear shoes on our feet."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which of these is a bird?','[{"id": "a", "text": "fish"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dog"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cow"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A hen is a bird that lays eggs."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','What is the opposite of ''big''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "small"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "round"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fast"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The opposite of big is small."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','What is the opposite of ''hot''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "dry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cold"}, {"id": "c", "text": "soft"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wet"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The opposite of hot is cold."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','What is the opposite of ''day''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "morning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sun"}, {"id": "c", "text": "night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "noon"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The opposite of day is night."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','What is the opposite of ''happy''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "sad"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kind"}, {"id": "c", "text": "clean"}, {"id": "d", "text": "young"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The opposite of happy is sad."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','What is the opposite of ''open''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "push"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shut"}, {"id": "c", "text": "empty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "full"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The opposite of open is shut (closed)."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word in this sentence is a naming word (noun): ''The dog is running.''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "the"}, {"id": "b", "text": "is"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dog"}, {"id": "d", "text": "running"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Dog'' is a naming word, the name of an animal."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which of these words is the name of a place?','[{"id": "a", "text": "jump"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lagos"}, {"id": "c", "text": "quickly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "blue"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Lagos is the name of a city, so it is a naming word."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which of these is a naming word?','[{"id": "a", "text": "sing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "under"}, {"id": "d", "text": "run"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Table'' is a naming word for a thing."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word names a person?','[{"id": "a", "text": "teacher"}, {"id": "b", "text": "eat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fast"}, {"id": "d", "text": "on"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Teacher'' is the name of a person."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Which word is an action word: ''The boy will ____ the ball.''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "kick"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chair"}, {"id": "c", "text": "red"}, {"id": "d", "text": "box"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Kick'' is an action word that tells what the boy does."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Choose the correct word: ''Musa and I ____ friends.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "is"}, {"id": "b", "text": "are"}, {"id": "c", "text": "am"}, {"id": "d", "text": "be"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We use ''are'' with more than one person."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Which word can take the place of ''Amaka'' in: ''Amaka is my sister. ____ is kind.''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "He"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It"}, {"id": "c", "text": "She"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We use ''She'' for a girl or woman like Amaka."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Which of these is an action word?','[{"id": "a", "text": "jump"}, {"id": "b", "text": "house"}, {"id": "c", "text": "green"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Jump'' is an action word; it tells what someone does."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Which word can take the place of ''the boys'' in: ''The boys are playing. ____ are happy.''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "She"}, {"id": "b", "text": "He"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "We use ''They'' for more than one person."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which of these is a complete sentence?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The cat is sleeping."}, {"id": "b", "text": "under the big"}, {"id": "c", "text": "running fast and"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a red ball on"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''The cat is sleeping.'' is a full sentence with a clear meaning."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Complete the sentence: ''I ____ rice for lunch.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "eat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chair"}, {"id": "c", "text": "blue"}, {"id": "d", "text": "under"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Eat'' is the action word that makes the sentence complete."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which mark should end this sentence: ''We are going to school''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "a comma (,)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a full stop (.)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a letter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a number"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A telling sentence ends with a full stop."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which word correctly begins this sentence: ''____ sun is very hot today.''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Run"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Eat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blue"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''The'' correctly starts the sentence about the sun."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Complete the sentence: ''The bird can ____ in the sky.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "fly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cup"}, {"id": "c", "text": "door"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tall"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Fly'' is the correct action word for a bird in the sky."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Read: ''Ngozi has a red cap. She wears it to school.'' What colour is Ngozi''s cap?','[{"id": "a", "text": "blue"}, {"id": "b", "text": "green"}, {"id": "c", "text": "red"}, {"id": "d", "text": "black"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The passage says Ngozi has a red cap."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Read: ''Tunde likes to play football with his friends after school.'' What does Tunde like to play?','[{"id": "a", "text": "football"}, {"id": "b", "text": "drums"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cards"}, {"id": "d", "text": "chess"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The passage says Tunde likes to play football."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Read: ''Mama went to the market to buy fish and pepper.'' What did Mama go to buy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "books and pens"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fish and pepper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shoes and cap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rice and beans"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The passage says Mama went to buy fish and pepper."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Read: ''The rain fell heavily, so the children stayed inside the house.'' Why did the children stay inside?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They were tired"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It was dark"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The rain fell heavily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They were hungry"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The passage says the children stayed inside because the rain fell heavily."}',0.3,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Read: ''Chidi has three goats. He feeds them every morning.'' How many goats does Chidi have?','[{"id": "a", "text": "two"}, {"id": "b", "text": "three"}, {"id": "c", "text": "four"}, {"id": "d", "text": "five"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The passage says Chidi has three goats."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','What do you say to your teacher when you arrive in the morning?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Good morning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Good night"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Goodbye"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Well done"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We greet ''Good morning'' early in the day."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','What do you say when someone gives you a gift?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Go away"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thank you"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Good night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sorry"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "We say ''Thank you'' to show we are grateful."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','What do you say when you want to ask for something politely?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Please"}, {"id": "b", "text": "No"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Now"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We use ''Please'' to ask politely."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','What do you say when you step on someone''s foot by mistake?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Welcome"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hello"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sorry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Yes"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We say ''Sorry'' to apologise for a mistake."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','What greeting do you use when going to bed at night?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Good afternoon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Good morning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Good night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Well done"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We say ''Good night'' before sleeping."}',0.2,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P2','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','Which question asks for a person''s name?','[{"id": "a", "text": "What is your name?"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Where is the ball?"}, {"id": "c", "text": "How old is the tree?"}, {"id": "d", "text": "What time is it?"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''What is your name?'' asks a person to tell their name."}',0.25,'{P2,ENG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
