  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T3','NLG-T3-O2','In Hausa, "uwa" means what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "father"}, {"id": "b", "text": "child"}, {"id": "c", "text": "mother"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sister"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "\"Uwa\" means mother in Hausa."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T3','NLG-T3-O2','In Igbo, the word for "child" is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "nna"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nne"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nwa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nwoke"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "\"Nwa\" means child in Igbo."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T3','NLG-T3-O2','In Yoruba, "omo" means what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "mother"}, {"id": "b", "text": "father"}, {"id": "c", "text": "child"}, {"id": "d", "text": "house"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "\"Omo\" means child in Yoruba."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','The proverb "Ise ni oogun ise", meaning hard work cures poverty, is in which language?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "d", "text": "English"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "\"Ise ni oogun ise\" is a Yoruba proverb about hard work."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','The Igbo proverb "Egbe bere ugo bere" (let the kite perch and the eagle perch) teaches us to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "fight always"}, {"id": "b", "text": "live and let others live"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sleep early"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eat a lot"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "It teaches fairness and living together in peace."}',0.35,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','The Hausa saying "Hankuri maganin duniya" means patience is the medicine of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "the farm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the world"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the school"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "\"Hankuri maganin duniya\" means patience is the medicine of the world."}',0.35,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','Using proverbs to teach respect for elders is a custom found in which Nigerian cultures?','[{"id": "a", "text": "only Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "only Igbo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only Hausa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "all three cultures"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "Yoruba, Igbo and Hausa cultures all use proverbs to teach respect."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O1','The Yoruba proverb about not pointing to your father''s house with the left hand teaches:','[{"id": "a", "text": "counting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "respect and good manners"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cooking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "singing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "It teaches respect and good manners."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','A proverb is a wise saying that teaches a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "song"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lesson"}, {"id": "c", "text": "game"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A proverb is a wise saying that teaches a lesson."}',0.2,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','The Yoruba proverb "Ise ni oogun ise" encourages children to be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "lazy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hardworking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rude"}, {"id": "d", "text": "greedy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "It encourages children to work hard."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','The Hausa saying about patience teaches us to be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "patient"}, {"id": "b", "text": "angry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "noisy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hasty"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Hausa saying teaches us to be patient."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','The Igbo proverb "Egbe bere ugo bere" teaches people to live in:','[{"id": "a", "text": "fear"}, {"id": "b", "text": "peace and fairness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "anger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hunger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "It teaches people to live in peace and fairness."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T4','NLG-T4-O2','Proverbs in Nigerian languages are mostly used by elders to teach good:','[{"id": "a", "text": "manners and wisdom"}, {"id": "b", "text": "football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cooking only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "drawing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Elders use proverbs to teach good manners and wisdom."}',0.2,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','In Yoruba culture, a boy greets an elder by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "waving"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prostrating (dobale)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shouting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "running away"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A Yoruba boy prostrates (dobale) to greet an elder respectfully."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','In Yoruba culture, a girl shows respect to an elder by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "kneeling (kunle)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "jumping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "clapping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "whistling"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A Yoruba girl kneels (kunle) to greet an elder respectfully."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','The flowing gown called "babban riga" is a traditional attire worn mostly by the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Efik"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The \"babban riga\" is a traditional Hausa attire."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','In Yoruba culture, the traditional cap worn by men is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "fila"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gida"}, {"id": "c", "text": "oji"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nri"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The \"fila\" is the traditional Yoruba cap for men."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O1','The patterned "isiagu" shirt is a traditional attire worn by the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa men"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Igbo men"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fulani girls"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ijaw fishermen"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The \"isiagu\" is worn by Igbo men, often chiefs and titled men."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The New Yam Festival (Iri Ji) is celebrated mainly by the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ibibio"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The New Yam Festival (Iri Ji) is an important Igbo celebration."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The Durbar festival, famous for its horse riders, is celebrated mainly in which part of Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "the Igbo East"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the Hausa North"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the Yoruba West"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the Niger Delta"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Durbar festival is celebrated in the Hausa North."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','Breaking the kola nut (oji) to welcome guests is an important custom among the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fulani"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Breaking kola nut (oji) is an important Igbo welcome custom."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The Eyo festival is celebrated in which Yoruba city?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kano"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lagos"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Enugu"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Aba"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Eyo festival is a famous Yoruba celebration in Lagos."}',0.3,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P3','NLG','NLG-T5','NLG-T5-O2','The Sallah celebration is an important festival among many:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa Muslims"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Igbo traders"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Yoruba farmers only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ijaw fishermen"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sallah is widely celebrated among Hausa Muslims in the North."}',0.25,'{P3,NLG,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O1','Which part of the computer is used to type letters and numbers?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Printer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The keyboard has keys used to type letters, numbers and symbols into the computer."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O1','The part of the computer that looks like a television screen and shows pictures and words is the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "System unit"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The monitor displays what the computer is doing, much like a television screen."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O1','Which device is used to point at and select things on the computer screen?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scanner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Speaker"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The mouse is used to move the pointer and click on items on the screen."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O1','Amaka wants to hear the sound from a song on the computer. Which part will she use?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Monitor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Speakers produce sound so that we can hear music and other audio from the computer."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O1','The box that holds the main working parts of the computer, like the brain, is called the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "System unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mouse"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The system unit is the case that holds the main parts that make the computer work."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O2','Which of these is an input device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Speaker"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A keyboard sends information into the computer, so it is an input device."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O2','Which of these is an output device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Scanner"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A printer gives out results from the computer as printed paper, so it is an output device."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O2','A device that puts information INTO the computer is called a/an?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Output device"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Input device"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Storage box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Power device"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Input devices are used to enter data and instructions into the computer."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O2','Which pair contains only input devices?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keyboard and mouse"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitor and printer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speaker and monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Printer and keyboard"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Both the keyboard and the mouse send information into the computer."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T1','BDL-T1-O2','The monitor is best described as a/an?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Input device"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Output device"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Typing device"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pointing device"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The monitor shows results from the computer, so it is an output device."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O1','What should you do to your hands before using a computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rub oil on them"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make sure they are clean and dry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wet them with water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cover them with sand"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clean and dry hands keep the keyboard and mouse safe from dirt and damage."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O1','Why should you not eat or drink close to a computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The food may spill and damage the computer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The computer will eat the food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Food makes the computer faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It makes the screen bigger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Spilled food or drink can enter the computer and damage its parts."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O1','To rest your eyes while using the computer for a long time, you should?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Look away from the screen from time to time"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Move the screen very close to your eyes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Turn off all the lights in the room"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stare without blinking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Looking away regularly gives your eyes rest and protects them from strain."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O1','How should you sit when using a computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Lie down on the floor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sit upright with a straight back"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bend very low over the keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stand on the chair"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sitting upright with a straight back protects your body from aches and pain."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O1','What should you do if you see torn or exposed electrical wires near the computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Touch the wires to test them"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pour water on the wires"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tell a teacher or adult at once"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cover the wires with paper and use the computer"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Reporting damaged wires to an adult keeps everyone safe from electric shock."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O2','What is used to protect a computer from dust when it is not in use?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A dust cover"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A bowl of water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A basket of fruit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A wet cloth left on it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A dust cover keeps dust away and keeps the computer clean."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O2','The correct way to turn off a computer is to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pull out the power cable suddenly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Use the shut down command properly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hit the monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pour water on it"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Using the shut down command closes the computer safely without damage."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O2','Why should a computer be kept in a cool, airy place?','[{"id": "a", "text": "So that it does not get too hot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "So that it can swim"}, {"id": "c", "text": "So that it grows bigger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "So that it can eat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Keeping the computer cool prevents it from overheating and getting damaged."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O2','To clean the surface of a computer screen, you should use a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wet dripping rag"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Soft dry cloth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sharp knife"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bucket of sand"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A soft dry cloth cleans the screen gently without scratching or wetting it."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T2','BDL-T2-O2','During a sudden power surge, a device that helps protect the computer is the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stabiliser or surge protector"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ceiling fan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kitchen stove"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Television remote"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stabiliser or surge protector guards the computer against harmful changes in electric power."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O1','Which key is used to create a space between words while typing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Enter key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spacebar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shift key"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Delete key"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The spacebar is the long key at the bottom used to make spaces between words."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O1','Which key is used to remove a letter to the left of the cursor?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Backspace key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spacebar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shift key"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Caps Lock key"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The backspace key deletes the character just before the cursor."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O1','To type a capital letter for one word, you hold down the Shift key and press the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Number key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spacebar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Letter key"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Enter key"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Holding Shift while pressing a letter key gives the capital form of that letter."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O1','Which key moves the cursor to start a new line?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Enter key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shift key"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Backspace key"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Caps Lock key"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Enter key ends the current line and starts a new one."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O1','When the Caps Lock key is turned on, the letters you type will be?','[{"id": "a", "text": "All small letters"}, {"id": "b", "text": "All capital letters"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only numbers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blank spaces"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Caps Lock makes every letter you type appear as a capital letter."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O2','Pressing the left mouse button once quickly is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clicking"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Dragging"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Scrolling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Typing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pressing the left mouse button once is known as clicking."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O2','To open a file or program, you usually?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Double-click on it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blow on the screen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shake the mouse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Press the spacebar many times"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Double-clicking, two quick clicks, is the common way to open files and programs."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O2','The small arrow that moves on the screen when you move the mouse is called the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pointer or cursor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Button"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Window"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Speaker"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The pointer, also called the cursor, shows where the mouse is on the screen."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O2','Chidi wants to move an icon from one place to another on the screen. He should?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Click, hold, and drag it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shout at the icon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Turn off the computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Press Caps Lock"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dragging means holding the button down while moving the mouse to a new place."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T3','BDL-T3-O2','The part of the mouse used to move up and down a long page is the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Scroll wheel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spacebar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Screen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Power button"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The scroll wheel in the middle of the mouse helps you move up and down a page."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O1','A word processor is a program used mainly to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Type and store words and documents"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Play football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cook food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Draw only pictures"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A word processor is used to type, edit and store written work like letters and stories."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O1','Which of these is an example of a word processing program?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Word"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A wall clock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A pencil sharpener"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A pair of scissors"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Microsoft Word is a popular word processing program used to type documents."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O1','Ngozi wants to type a letter to her aunty in Lagos on the computer. The best program to use is a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Word processor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Calculator"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Music player"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Camera"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A word processor is designed for typing letters and other written documents."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O1','The blinking line that shows where your text will appear when you type is called the?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cursor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Button"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cable"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The blinking cursor shows the exact place where the next letter will appear."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O1','One good reason for using a word processor instead of writing by hand is that you can?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Easily correct mistakes before printing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the paper heavier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop electricity from working"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Turn words into food"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A word processor lets you edit and correct your work neatly before printing it."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O2','After typing a document, what should you do so that you do not lose your work?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Save the document"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Delete the document"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Turn off the light"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Close your eyes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Saving keeps your work stored so you can open it again later."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O2','To make a paper copy of your typed document, you should?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Print it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fold the monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shake the mouse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sing to it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Printing sends the document to the printer to produce a copy on paper."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O2','When you save a document, you should give it a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "File name"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cup of water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "New keyboard"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A file name helps you find and open the document again later."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O2','Which device must be connected and switched on before you can print your work?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mouse only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ceiling fan"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The printer is the device that produces the paper copy of your document."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T4','BDL-T4-O2','To start typing a fresh piece of work, you should open a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "New document"}, {"id": "b", "text": "New window in the wall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bottle of ink"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bag of rice"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Opening a new document gives you a blank page to begin typing."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O1','The internet is best described as a large network that connects?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Computers all over the world"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Only chairs and tables"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only one classroom"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buckets of water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The internet links computers around the world so they can share information."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O1','Which of these can you do on the internet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Search for information"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cook jollof rice"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sweep the floor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Iron your clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The internet lets you search for and read information on many topics."}',0.3,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O1','A program used to open websites and browse the internet is called a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Web browser"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Frying pan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Calculator"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Broom"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A web browser, such as Chrome, is used to open websites on the internet."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O1','Sending a letter to a friend quickly through the internet can be done using?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Email"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A wooden spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A candle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A watering can"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Email lets you send written messages to people through the internet."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O1','To connect to the internet, a computer usually needs?','[{"id": "a", "text": "An internet connection such as Wi-Fi or data"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A plate of food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A football boot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A box of chalk"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A computer needs an internet connection like Wi-Fi or mobile data to go online."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O2','You should NOT share which of these with strangers online?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Your home address and phone number"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The name of your favourite colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A drawing of a flower"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The number of days in a week"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Personal details like your address and phone number should be kept private online."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O2','If a stranger online asks to meet you in person, you should?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tell a trusted adult and not go"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Go alone at once"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Give them your school address"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Keep it a secret from your parents"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Telling a trusted adult keeps you safe from strangers who may want to harm you."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O2','A password that keeps your account safe should be?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kept secret and not shared"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Written on the school wall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shouted to everyone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Given to strangers online"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A password must be kept secret so that others cannot use your account."}',0.35,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O2','If you see something rude or frightening on the internet, the best thing to do is?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tell a parent or teacher at once"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keep looking at it for a long time"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Send it to your friends"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Copy it into your notebook"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Telling a trusted adult helps you handle upsetting content safely."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BDL','BDL-T5','BDL-T5-O2','Which of these is a safe habit when using the internet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Asking an adult before opening strange links"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clicking every advert you see"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Giving out your password freely"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chatting with strangers in secret"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Asking an adult before opening strange links helps protect you from harmful content."}',0.4,'{P4,BDL,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O1','Which of the following is a living thing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A stone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A table"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A bucket"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A goat can grow, move, feed and reproduce, so it is a living thing."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O1','One characteristic that all living things share is the ability to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rust when wet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Grow and reproduce"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Melt in the sun"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Float on water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Living things grow and reproduce, unlike non-living things."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O1','Which of these is a non-living thing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A mango tree"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A fish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A plastic chair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A hen"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A plastic chair does not feed, grow or reproduce, so it is non-living."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O1','Amaka saw something in the compound that was breathing and moving on its own. It was most likely a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Broom"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lizard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bicycle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rock"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A lizard breathes and moves by itself because it is a living thing."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O1','Which activity can living things do but non-living things cannot?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Get bigger by growing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stay in one place"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change colour when painted"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Break into pieces"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Only living things grow bigger by themselves through feeding."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O2','Which of the following is a plant?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A dog"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A maize plant"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A cow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A snake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A maize plant is a plant because it makes its own food and is rooted to the ground."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O2','Which of these is an animal?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Orange tree"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Goat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Yam"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A goat is an animal because it moves about and feeds on plants."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O2','All living things need which of the following to stay alive?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Food and air"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Petrol and oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand and cement"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paper and ink"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Food and air are basic needs of all living things."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O2','Green plants are different from animals because plants can:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Run very fast"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make their own food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fly in the air"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sleep at night"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Green plants make their own food using sunlight, while animals cannot."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T1','BST-T1-O2','Musa keeps a hen at home. To keep the hen alive, he must give it:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Food and water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nails and wire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chalk and slate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sand and stones"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hen is a living animal that needs food and water to survive."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O1','Which gas in the air do humans and animals need to breathe in?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Carbon dioxide"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Oxygen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Smoke"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dust"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Humans and animals breathe in oxygen from the air to stay alive."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O1','We know that air is present around us because it can:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Be seen with the eyes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Move a flag or leaves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Be held in the hand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Turn into stone"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Moving air (wind) makes flags and leaves move, showing that air is around us."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O1','Pure water for drinking should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Coloured and smelly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clean and colourless"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Muddy and thick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Full of leaves"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clean, colourless and odourless water is safe for drinking."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O1','Which of the following is an important use of water at home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cooking food"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lighting a bulb"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sharpening a knife"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Playing football"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Water is used for cooking food, among many other home uses."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O1','Moving air is also called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rain"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wind"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fire"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Air in motion is known as wind."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O2','The three main types of soil are sandy soil, clay soil and:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cement soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plastic soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Glass soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The three main soil types are sandy, clay and loamy soil."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O2','Which type of soil is the best for growing most crops on a farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rocky soil"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Loamy soil holds water and nutrients well, so it is best for farming."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O2','A potter in the market uses which type of soil to make clay pots?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ash"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clay soil is sticky and can be moulded, so it is used to make pots."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O2','Sandy soil feels which way when you touch it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rough and gritty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Smooth and sticky"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Soft like cotton"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wet like oil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sandy soil is made of large grains, so it feels rough and gritty."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T2','BST-T2-O2','Which type of soil holds water for the longest time?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gravel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dust"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clay soil has tiny particles that trap water, so it holds water longest."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O1','Which material is used to make the frame of a window louvre?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rubber"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Metal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Paper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Metal is strong and long-lasting, so it is used for window frames."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O1','A carpenter in Enugu uses wood mainly to make:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Chairs and tables"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drinking water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Electric wire"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Car tyres"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Wood is used by carpenters to make furniture such as chairs and tables."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O1','Which material is used to make a car tyre?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Glass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rubber"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Paper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cotton"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rubber is stretchy and strong, so it is used to make tyres."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O1','Louvre blades in a window are usually made of glass because glass is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Transparent so light can pass through"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Soft like sponge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Able to bend easily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Good for eating"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Glass is transparent, allowing light to pass through the window."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O1','Which material is best for making a school notebook?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Metal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Paper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rubber"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Paper is light and easy to write on, so it is used for notebooks."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O2','Which of the following is a natural material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plastic"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wood"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rubber tyre"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Wood comes directly from trees, so it is a natural material."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O2','Which of these is a man-made (artificial) material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plastic"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Water"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Plastic is produced in factories, so it is a man-made material."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O2','Natural materials are those that:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Are made in factories"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Come from nature such as plants and animals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Are only found in shops"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cannot be used at all"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Natural materials come from nature, such as plants, animals and rocks."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O2','Which pair contains only natural materials?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton and leather"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Plastic and nylon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Glass and rubber band"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paper and biro"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cotton comes from plants and leather from animal skin, both natural."}',0.45,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T3','BST-T3-O2','Sand used for building comes from nature, so it is classified as a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Man-made material"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Natural material"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Living thing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Machine"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sand is taken directly from nature, so it is a natural material."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O1','Before eating food, you should always:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wash your hands with soap and water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rub your hands in the sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wipe your hands on your shirt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Do nothing at all"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Washing hands with soap and water removes germs before eating."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O1','How many times a day should you brush your teeth for good dental health?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Only once a week"}, {"id": "b", "text": "At least two times a day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Once a month"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Never"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Brushing at least twice daily keeps teeth clean and healthy."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O1','Cutting your finger nails regularly helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make you run faster"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keep germs from hiding under the nails"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Make your voice louder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Help you sleep"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dirt and germs collect under long nails, so trimming them keeps you clean."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O1','Which of these is a good personal hygiene habit?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bathing every day"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wearing dirty clothes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sharing a toothbrush"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Skipping your bath for a week"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bathing daily keeps the body clean and free from germs."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O1','Ngozi wants to keep her hair clean and neat. She should:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wash and comb it regularly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rub oil and sand in it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Never touch it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leave dust in it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Washing and combing the hair regularly keeps it clean and neat."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O2','Which insect spreads malaria in Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Housefly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mosquito"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Butterfly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ant"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The mosquito bites people and spreads the malaria parasite."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O2','Sleeping under a treated mosquito net helps to prevent:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Malaria"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Toothache"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A broken leg"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Poor eyesight"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The net stops mosquito bites, helping to prevent malaria."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O2','Drinking clean, boiled water helps to prevent diseases like:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cholera and typhoid"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Headache from noise"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sunburn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cut finger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cholera and typhoid spread through dirty water, so clean water prevents them."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O2','Covering your mouth when you cough or sneeze helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stop germs from spreading to others"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make you taller"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cool the room"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clean your teeth"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Covering the mouth traps germs and stops them spreading to others."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T4','BST-T4-O2','Which of these is the best way to keep the community free from diseases?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keeping the surroundings clean and clearing dirty water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Throwing refuse in the gutter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leaving food uncovered"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blocking all drains"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean environment with no stagnant water reduces disease-carrying pests."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O1','Which part of the computer is used to type letters and numbers?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Printer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The keyboard has keys used to type letters and numbers into the computer."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O1','The part of the computer that looks like a television screen and shows your work is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "System unit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The monitor displays what the computer is doing on its screen."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O1','Which device is moved with the hand to point and click on the screen?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Monitor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The mouse is used to point at and click items on the screen."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O1','Which part of the computer is used to produce documents on paper?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Monitor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The printer copies work from the computer onto paper."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O1','The main box that holds the working parts of a desktop computer is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "System unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mouse pad"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Screen"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The system unit houses the main parts that make the computer work."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O2','A computer can be used in the school to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Type and store pupils'' results"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cook the school lunch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sweep the classroom"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fetch water from the well"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Computers are used to type and store information such as pupils'' results."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O2','Which ICT device is commonly used to make phone calls and send text messages?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mobile phone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cooking pot"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hoe"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A mobile phone is an ICT device used for calls and text messages."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O2','In a bank in Lagos, computers are useful because they help to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keep records of customers'' money"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Plant crops on a farm"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cut people''s hair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wash the floor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Banks use computers to keep accurate records of customers'' money."}',0.4,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O2','A calculator is an ICT device that helps people to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Do sums quickly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Boil water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ride to school"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Grow plants"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A calculator is used to do calculations quickly and correctly."}',0.3,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','BST','BST-T5','BST-T5-O2','Which of these is a good use of the computer at home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watching lessons and playing learning games"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Frying akara"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grinding pepper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ironing clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Computers can be used at home to watch lessons and play learning games."}',0.35,'{P4,BST,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Ada woke up early, packed her bag, and hurried to catch the bus to school. What is Ada mainly getting ready to do?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Go to the market"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Go to school"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Visit her grandmother"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Play football"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "She packed her bag and rushed for the bus to school, so she is getting ready for school."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','The rain fell heavily all night in Lagos, so the streets were flooded by morning. What caused the flooded streets?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The hot sun"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A strong wind"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The heavy rain"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The busy traffic"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The passage says heavy rain fell all night, which caused the flooding."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Musa saved his pocket money for three weeks to buy a new football boot. What is the main idea of this sentence?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Musa likes to waste money"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Musa saved money to buy football boots"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Musa hates football"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Musa lost his money"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "He saved his pocket money for three weeks in order to buy football boots."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Our teacher told us that reading many books helps us to speak and write English well. According to the sentence, what helps us speak and write English well?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sleeping early"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Eating good food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reading many books"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Playing all day"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The teacher said reading many books helps with speaking and writing English."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O1','Ngozi swept the floor, washed the plates, and then rested. Which of these did Ngozi NOT do?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sweep the floor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wash the plates"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rest"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cook the rice"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "The sentence mentions sweeping, washing plates, and resting, but not cooking rice."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','The dark clouds gathered and thunder rolled across the sky. What is most likely going to happen next?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The sun will shine brightly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It will rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It will snow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The moon will appear"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dark clouds and thunder are signs that rain is about to fall."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','Emeka forgot to study for his test and could not answer the questions. How did Emeka most likely feel?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Happy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Excited"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Worried"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Proud"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Not being able to answer because he did not study would make Emeka worried."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','The word ''enormous'' in ''The elephant was an enormous animal'' means the same as which word?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tiny"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Very big"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Quick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clever"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An elephant is huge, so ''enormous'' means very big."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','Bola put on her raincoat and carried an umbrella before leaving home. What can we guess about the weather?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It was sunny"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It was raining or about to rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It was very dry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It was harmattan"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A raincoat and umbrella show that it was rainy weather."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T1','ENG-T1-O2','The hungry lion crept quietly toward the grazing antelope. What is the lion most likely about to do?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sleep under a tree"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hunt and catch the antelope"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Drink water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Play with the antelope"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A hungry lion creeping toward an antelope is preparing to hunt it."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which word in this sentence is a noun: ''The boy kicked the ball''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "kicked"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the"}, {"id": "c", "text": "boy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quickly"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Boy'' names a person, so it is a noun."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which of these words is a pronoun?','[{"id": "a", "text": "she"}, {"id": "b", "text": "table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "run"}, {"id": "d", "text": "happy"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''She'' takes the place of a noun, so it is a pronoun."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Choose the correct pronoun to complete the sentence: ''Chidi is my friend and ___ is very kind.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "they"}, {"id": "c", "text": "he"}, {"id": "d", "text": "we"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Chidi is one male person, so the correct pronoun is ''he''."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which word is a proper noun?','[{"id": "a", "text": "city"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Abuja"}, {"id": "c", "text": "river"}, {"id": "d", "text": "girl"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Abuja'' is the name of a particular place, so it is a proper noun."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O1','Which pronoun correctly replaces the underlined words: ''Aisha and I went to the farm''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They"}, {"id": "b", "text": "We"}, {"id": "c", "text": "You"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Aisha and I'' includes the speaker, so it is replaced by ''We''."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','Which word in this sentence is a verb: ''The children sang a song''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "children"}, {"id": "b", "text": "song"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sang"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Sang'' shows an action, so it is a verb."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','Which of these words is an adjective?','[{"id": "a", "text": "beautiful"}, {"id": "b", "text": "jump"}, {"id": "c", "text": "book"}, {"id": "d", "text": "she"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Beautiful'' describes a noun, so it is an adjective."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','Choose the adjective in this sentence: ''The tall man bought a hat.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "man"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bought"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hat"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Tall'' describes the man, so it is an adjective."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','Which word completes the sentence with a verb: ''The dog ___ loudly at the gate.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "brown"}, {"id": "b", "text": "barked"}, {"id": "c", "text": "quick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "big"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Barked'' is the action the dog does, so it is the verb."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T2','ENG-T2-O2','In the sentence ''Fatima wore a red dress'', which word is the adjective?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fatima"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wore"}, {"id": "c", "text": "red"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dress"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Red'' describes the colour of the dress, so it is an adjective."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word means the same as ''happy''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "sad"}, {"id": "b", "text": "glad"}, {"id": "c", "text": "angry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tired"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Glad'' has the same meaning as ''happy''."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word is the opposite of ''big''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "large"}, {"id": "b", "text": "huge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "small"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wide"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Small'' is the opposite of ''big''."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word means the same as ''quick''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "slow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fast"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "heavy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Fast'' has the same meaning as ''quick''."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word is the opposite of ''clean''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "neat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tidy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fresh"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Dirty'' is the opposite of ''clean''."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O1','Which word means the same as ''begin''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "stop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "end"}, {"id": "c", "text": "start"}, {"id": "d", "text": "close"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Start'' has the same meaning as ''begin''."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','A person who teaches pupils in school is called a ___.','[{"id": "a", "text": "farmer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "teacher"}, {"id": "c", "text": "driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "doctor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A teacher is the person who teaches pupils in school."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','The place where we buy and sell goods like yam and tomatoes is called a ___.','[{"id": "a", "text": "market"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hospital"}, {"id": "c", "text": "church"}, {"id": "d", "text": "library"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A market is where goods are bought and sold."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Choose the correct word: ''We use our ___ to hear sounds.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "eyes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nose"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ears"}, {"id": "d", "text": "legs"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "We hear sounds with our ears."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','A young cow is called a ___.','[{"id": "a", "text": "kid"}, {"id": "b", "text": "calf"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "puppy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The young one of a cow is called a calf."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T3','ENG-T3-O2','Choose the correct word: ''The nurse works in a ___.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "farm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hospital"}, {"id": "c", "text": "garage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "market"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nurse works in a hospital where sick people are cared for."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which sentence is punctuated correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "we are going to Kano tomorrow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "We are going to Kano tomorrow."}, {"id": "c", "text": "we are going to kano tomorrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "We are going to kano tomorrow"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "It begins with a capital letter, uses a capital K for Kano, and ends with a full stop."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which mark should end this question: ''What is your name''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Full stop (.)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Comma (,)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Question mark (?)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "No mark"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A question ends with a question mark."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which word should begin with a capital letter?','[{"id": "a", "text": "table"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nigeria"}, {"id": "c", "text": "book"}, {"id": "d", "text": "chair"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Nigeria'' is the name of a country, so it must start with a capital letter."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which punctuation mark shows strong feeling, as in ''What a lovely day''?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Full stop (.)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Exclamation mark (!)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Comma (,)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Question mark (?)"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An exclamation mark shows strong feeling or surprise."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O1','Which sentence uses capital letters correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "my friend chika lives in enugu."}, {"id": "b", "text": "My friend Chika lives in Enugu."}, {"id": "c", "text": "my friend Chika lives in enugu."}, {"id": "d", "text": "My friend chika lives in Enugu."}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The sentence starts with a capital, and ''Chika'' and ''Enugu'' are names needing capitals."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Which word is spelt correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "freind"}, {"id": "b", "text": "friend"}, {"id": "c", "text": "frend"}, {"id": "d", "text": "friynd"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The correct spelling is ''friend''."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Which word is spelt correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "school"}, {"id": "b", "text": "skool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "schul"}, {"id": "d", "text": "scool"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The correct spelling is ''school''."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Which word is spelt correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "beautifull"}, {"id": "b", "text": "beutiful"}, {"id": "c", "text": "beautiful"}, {"id": "d", "text": "beatiful"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The correct spelling is ''beautiful''."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T4','ENG-T4-O2','Which word is spelt correctly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "tomorow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tommorow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tomorrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tomarow"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The correct spelling is ''tomorrow''."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','Which of these is a complete sentence?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The big dog"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Running to school"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The cat drank the milk."}, {"id": "d", "text": "Under the table"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''The cat drank the milk.'' has a subject and a verb and expresses a complete thought."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','Arrange these words into a correct sentence: ''plays / Tunde / football''.','[{"id": "a", "text": "Football Tunde plays"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tunde plays football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plays football Tunde"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Football plays Tunde"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Tunde plays football'' follows the correct subject-verb-object order."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','Which word correctly joins the two ideas: ''I was tired ___ I went to bed.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "but"}, {"id": "b", "text": "so"}, {"id": "c", "text": "or"}, {"id": "d", "text": "if"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''So'' shows that being tired is the reason for going to bed."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','Which sentence is written in the correct order?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rice ate Ngozi the"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ngozi ate the rice"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ate the rice Ngozi"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The rice Ngozi ate"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "''Ngozi ate the rice'' has the correct subject-verb-object order."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O1','Which word best completes the sentence: ''The pupils are quiet ___ the teacher is talking.''','[{"id": "a", "text": "because"}, {"id": "b", "text": "banana"}, {"id": "c", "text": "table"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quickly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Because'' shows the reason the pupils are quiet."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','Which sentence is the best opening for a letter to a friend?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Goodbye and take care."}, {"id": "b", "text": "How are you and your family?"}, {"id": "c", "text": "I have finished my story."}, {"id": "d", "text": "The end."}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A friendly greeting like asking about the family is a good way to begin a letter."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','When writing about ''My School Day'', which sentence should come FIRST?','[{"id": "a", "text": "At last, the closing bell rang and we went home."}, {"id": "b", "text": "In the morning, I woke up and got ready for school."}, {"id": "c", "text": "During break, we ate our food."}, {"id": "d", "text": "In class, the teacher taught us mathematics."}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Waking up in the morning happens first, so it should begin the story."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','Which title is best for a composition about a person you love?','[{"id": "a", "text": "My Best Friend"}, {"id": "b", "text": "How to Ride a Bicycle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The Rainy Season"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A Visit to the Zoo"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''My Best Friend'' is about a person you love, so it fits the topic."}',0.3,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','Which sentence is the best way to END a story?','[{"id": "a", "text": "One sunny morning, I set out for the farm."}, {"id": "b", "text": "First, I greeted my mother."}, {"id": "c", "text": "Finally, we all went home happily."}, {"id": "d", "text": "My name is Amina."}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "''Finally, we all went home happily'' brings the story to a close."}',0.4,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','ENG','ENG-T5','ENG-T5-O2','In a story, which word helps to show that one event happened after another?','[{"id": "a", "text": "then"}, {"id": "b", "text": "green"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "happy"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "''Then'' shows the order of events, that one thing happened after another."}',0.35,'{P4,ENG,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','MTH','MTH-T1','MTH-T1-O1','In the number 4 786, what is the value of the digit 7?','[{"id": "a", "text": "7"}, {"id": "b", "text": "70"}, {"id": "c", "text": "700"}, {"id": "d", "text": "7 000"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The digit 7 is in the hundreds place, so its value is 7 x 100 = 700."}',0.3,'{P4,MTH,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','MTH','MTH-T1','MTH-T1-O1','How is the number 3 052 written in words?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Three hundred and fifty-two"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Three thousand and fifty-two"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Three thousand five hundred and two"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Thirty thousand and fifty-two"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "3 052 has 3 thousands, 0 hundreds, 5 tens and 2 units, read as three thousand and fifty-two."}',0.35,'{P4,MTH,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','MTH','MTH-T1','MTH-T1-O1','Which digit is in the thousands place in the number 8 419?','[{"id": "a", "text": "8"}, {"id": "b", "text": "4"}, {"id": "c", "text": "1"}, {"id": "d", "text": "9"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In 8 419, the digit 8 sits in the thousands place."}',0.28,'{P4,MTH,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
  ('P4','MTH','MTH-T1','MTH-T1-O1','What is the number ''six thousand, three hundred and forty'' written in figures?','[{"id": "a", "text": "6 034"}, {"id": "b", "text": "6 304"}, {"id": "c", "text": "6 340"}, {"id": "d", "text": "6 430"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Six thousands (6 000) plus three hundreds (300) plus forty (40) gives 6 340."}',0.35,'{P4,MTH,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v1}'),
